    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d131">

                <pb facs="0267" n="173" xml:id="pg173"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.348 Z 4/139: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kellogg</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-02-13T13:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 13,
                                1924—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 2:22 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>56. My 434, October 11, 4 p.m.,<anchor n="93" xml:id="d131-f1"/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">re</hi> flight of airship <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ZR</hi> [–<hi rendition="#italic">3</hi>]. Foreign Office desires to know
                    nationality and ownership of airship and [<hi rendition="#italic">at?</hi>] the
                    time of her flight from Friedrichshafen to the United States and whether she is
                    to be considered a civil or military airship.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d131-f1" n="93" xml:id="d131-f1-content">
                <p>“Your unnumbered instruction September 18. The Foreign Office desires to know
                    whether <hi rendition="#italic">ZR–3</hi> will be delivered to the United States
                    in Germany or in America. Harvey.” (File no. 811.348 Z 4/50.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
